    <statement><p>Consider the curve
    <m>\displaystyle  \mathbf{r} = 
(e^{-2 t} \cos(6 t), e^{-2 t} \sin(6 t), e^{-2 t})</m>.</p>
<p>Compute the arclength function <m>s(t)</m>: (with initial point <m>t=0</m>).</p>
<p><fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{6.63325\mathopen{}\left(\exp\mathopen{}\left(-2t\right)-1\right)}{-2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
